Z||000012||Sleeper||12-16-2000||10:43 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Master_Sushi:<BR><B>LOL, that looks about as good as the new "gone in 60 seconds".    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Gone In 60 Seconds is the main reason over the making of this movie The Fast and The Furious.  When 60 seconds came out the import guys were kinda mad that "there wasn't enough imports" in the movie and that the general focus was on the GT 500 Mustang.(i think its because the honda got smoked by the porsche in the begining, j/k) no but really, I have some friends with imports and though they did like the movie they thought there should have been some imports in the movie cuz they are the new trend in todays cars.  So anyways I heard that they were going to do the casting of cars here in L.A. and since L.A. is like the mecca for ricers they opened up the auditions for anybody with a souped up import, heard there was like hundreds of ricers, my friend Kevin went down to audition with his Corrado which is pretty fast(runs 11's) and was declined. He later found out that they want the mega-mega ricer look with the full on body kit, spoilers, loud exhaust, stickers, etc, etc.  <P>So what I'm getting at is the movie will probably be "Fast and Furious" (meaning good racing action like 60 seconds) but look for import racers with more show than go smoking domestics or something of that nature.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Sleeper (edited 12-16-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000013||Will||12-16-2000||11:23 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Uaana:<BR><B>Now they will think that they are really fast.  Don't belive me check out the website.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.thefastandthefurious.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thefastandthefurious.com</A> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm just posting this link so that I can download the trailer in the background then do with it as I please. Whoever programmed that webpage is a moron.<P><A HREF="http://www.thefastandthefurious.com/ff_mp_large.asx" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thefastandthefurious.com/ff_mp_large.asx</A><P>Nevermind, that didn't work<p>[This message has been edited by Will (edited 12-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||count_iblis||12-17-2000||09:17 AM||||The Honda was smoked by a Porsche?  Did I miss that?  It was a dead even race until the Honda slammed the brakes on becuase of the Police Officer at the light. That is one episode my friends and I always talk about.  Because we always wanted to know what was in it. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Sleeper||12-17-2000||11:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by count_iblis:<BR><B>The Honda was smoked by a Porsche?  Did I miss that?  It was a dead even race until the Honda slammed the brakes on becuase of the Police Officer at the light. That is one episode my friends and I always talk about.  Because we always wanted to know what was in it. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats what i'm talking about...though in this new movie it probably going to be the the other way around alot of overdubbing to make cars go faster than they are. <P>come on man, the porsche did have a foot or three on the honda I just exaggerated the "smoked" part though the porsche did smoke the honda off the line.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Standard||12-18-2000||01:54 AM||||There was alot of overdubbing going on in Gone in 60 Seconds, too.  In the flood canal scene, the cars never really got above 50-60 mph.  It was filmed at 12 or 16 frames per second, don't remember the exact number.  <P>Fast and Furious actually looks pretty cool.. and riced up imports are what most kids think are "cool" now anyways...  But as long as there's some good racing action it's fine with me.  <P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 153,000 miles and some busted up ground f/x  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redface.gif"> <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Greg Piet||12-18-2000||06:04 AM||||Well there is one automotive movie I will not be seeing.<BR>I cannot support the movie industry in giving the delusion that a coffee can and a wright brothers wing can compare/surpass american muscle...<P>I just thought it was cheesy, till I saw a good olde muscle car flip and lose to a ricer(unfortunately I did the low quality and couldnt make out the black muscle car).<P>Now kids are getting yet another source of misinformation...  grrrrrrr.<P>I must tell myself "Breathe in Greg... It will al be OK...  Theres no place like home Theres no place like home"||||reg||1
